                'The defence says nothing at all about paragraph 7, but sets out a full positive case on the same issue elsewhere.',
                'The defendant genuinely has no idea whether the plaintiff paid the third party, and wants to put the plaintiff to proof.',
                'The defendant knows for a fact the meeting never took place, and the defence says he "does not admit" it.',
                'The defendant has an unliquidated cross-claim for defective work and wants it both to reduce the claim and to stand as a claim of its own.',
                'The defendant pleads tender before action and has paid nothing into court.',
                'The defence and counterclaim are served as two separate documents.',
                'The counterclaim is against the plaintiff and a company that is not yet a party and is said to be liable along with the plaintiff.',
